From b8e7005cc5dfbabb0ba3eef0e91779dc97ad5426 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:24:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: image library: share: and usb: sources (folders
 used in place)

Stage 6.2, first part (cosmosex-floppy-library.md): share:<path> and
usb:<serial>:<path> sources of IMAGELIB_SOURCES are now loaded.

- A folder with an imagelist.csv (legacy format) uses that list; its file
  column is a path relative to the folder (no "..", no absolute paths, no
  URLs).
- A folder without a list is scanned for .st, .msa and .zip (up to 8
  levels, 20000 images, dot-folders skipped); the file name is the title.
- Their images are used where they are, without a download:
  ImageStorage::getImageLocalPath() asks the image list first, so the web
  API, the Atari config screen and "downloaded" markers all see them as
  available.
- The same image name (case-insensitive, without .zip/.st/.msa) from
  several sources is listed once, from the first source in
  IMAGELIB_SOURCES that has it.
- A source whose drive isn't attached is "unavailable" and its images
  aren't listed; the list is loaded again when the drive appears or the
  folder or its list changes.
- The list version for updates comes from web lists only.

Not yet: the 16 MB unpack cache and save copies (6.2/6.4): zipped images
from a folder are unpacked as before, and writes to a plain image from a
library folder go to that file, as for any image on a USB drive.
